Help The Hive — recipe import service
=====================================

This service is derived from Recipe Extractor:

    https://github.com/sleeper/recipe-extractor
    Copyright (c) 2024 Frederick Ros
    Licensed under the MIT License.

What was carried over, in substance:

  * the order of preference for obtaining a transcript — post description,
    then existing captions in their original language, then Whisper
    transcription of the downloaded audio (`transcripts.py`, derived from
    upstream `video_transcripts.py`);
  * the anti-hallucination framing of the extraction prompt, which is the
    most valuable idea in the original (`extract.py`);
  * the Markdown rendering of an extracted recipe (`markdown.py`);
  * the shape of the command line interface (`cli.py`).

What is new here:

  * output conforms to the Standard HTH Recipe Object in
    packages/api-contract/meals.graphql, rather than a flat recipe shape;
  * absence is recorded rather than filled — missingInformation,
    ValueConfidence, and baseMealPlanEligible;
  * a job-based HTTP API, service authentication, a source allowlist, a
    duration cap, per-import temporary directories, and provenance.

